{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2254","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2254","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2254\",\"parent_revision\":\"340c507f73705b4a3075a9c4a9c710bd22091474c8a3d6521e73bf8e15900496\",\"root_revision\":\"340c507f73705b4a3075a9c4a9c710bd22091474c8a3d6521e73bf8e15900496\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **code-review: architecture audit skill that emits mermaid module-dependency graph with severity color-coding** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/coding-agents/brooks-lint.md \u2014 pattern: Architecture Audit Mermaid dependency graph\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-10\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/agents/codebase-analyzer.md` and `code-reviewer.md` produce textual reports. Neither generates a visual dependency graph. There is no skill named `architecture-audit`, `architecture-graph`, `dependency-graph`, or similar in `plugins/development-harness/skills/`:\\n\\n```bash\\nls plugins/development-harness/skills/ | grep -iE \\\"architecture|graph|dependency\\\"\\n# returns nothing\\n```\\n\\nCircular dependency detection, dependency direction analysis, and module-level coupling visualization are not part of any current local workflow. The `/code-review-shared` skill (proposed in #2250) could host this as a sibling capability.\\n\\nbrooks-lint Mode 2 (Architecture Audit, README.md lines 109\u2013145) generates a native Mermaid flowchart of module dependencies with color-coded severity (red = circular dep / critical, yellow = warning, green = clean). Renders directly in GitHub, Notion, and Markdown without extra tools.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA new skill `plugins/development-harness/skills/code-review-architecture/SKILL.md` exists. It instructs the agent to:\\n\\n1. Build a module dependency graph from import/include relationships in the project source\\n2. Detect circular dependencies\\n3. Output a Mermaid `flowchart` with nodes color-coded by finding severity (red = circular dep / critical, yellow = warning, green = clean)\\n4. Register the Mermaid block as part of the `codebase-analysis` artifact\\n\\nThe skill is loadable independently and is invoked when a task asks for architecture review.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n```bash\\nls plugins/development-harness/skills/code-review-architecture/SKILL.md\\n```\\n\\nexists. Running the skill against a sample project produces an artifact containing a fenced ` ```mermaid ` block with `flowchart` keyword and at least one `style {node} fill:#` directive demonstrating severity color-coding.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"6f068c3f843f4c9e4c6ead96637bbf1e5131fa2ca2554636664e62129fc7ddb4\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCUJGg\"}"}